# ── RedBlue AI superproject .gitignore (plan 01 §6.3) ──
# The three engines (Decepticon / vigil / vigil-llm) are now VENDORED here as a self-contained
# deployable (source only — their venv/node_modules/.env stay ignored by the patterns below).
# They were previously reproduced by setup.sh from manifest.toml; that path still works to refresh them.

# Python envs / build
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Node
**/node_modules/
**/frontend/build/
**/frontend/dist/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/

# Secrets / env (never commit; *.example IS committed)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/env.example
deploy/.env

# Runtime / evidence spill
**/logs/
**/.dogfood/
**/workspace/
telemetry/**/data/
**/coordinator_data/
*.pcap
# …but **/logs/ and **/workspace/ above must NOT swallow application SOURCE under webapp/src:
# Next.js API-route dirs literally named logs/ or workspace/ are code there, not runtime spill.
# Targeted to those dir names only, so nested node_modules/.vite build junk stays ignored.
!webapp/src/**/logs/
!webapp/src/**/logs/**
!webapp/src/**/workspace/
!webapp/src/**/workspace/**

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code local settings (per-user; never commit)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Wazuh TLS certs — generated per-deploy by `make certs`, never commit
telemetry/wazuh/certs/
